From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 03:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] J604 local build: let the platform name the
 keyboard-backlight timeout

The idle.keyboardBacklight timeout (PR 12558) is opt-in per user in
shell.json, which the shell never deep-merges, so neither a fresh install
nor an existing one can get a machine's default from the package that
knows the machine. A platform package now names it as data in the fixed
platform root, /usr/share/omarchy-platform/idle.json
({"keyboardBacklight": <seconds>}), read like audio.json: shell.json's
value wins, 0 included, and without either the timeout stays off.

The timeout runs only where a *kbd_backlight* LED exists, so a platform
default reaches desktops without one as a no-op. When the timeout comes
on (session start, once the LED is found) the service runs restore, which
brings back a level a blank left dark across a reboot and does nothing
otherwise.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
